<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<sample title="First-Person Controller">
	<sdk_desc>Implementation of a first-person character controller with an advanced movement system and collision detection.</sdk_desc>
	<desc>
		<brief>
			<para>This sample demonstrates a first-person character controller implemented as a component attached to a <ui>PlayerDummy</ui>.</para>
			<para>The controller uses <link to="physics_collision" offset="collision_types">Shape-Surface</link> collisions to detect ground, walls, and slopes, and applies slope-aware movement to ensure stable walking on inclined geometry. It supports walking, running, jumping, air movement, smooth crouching, and camera rotation with vertical limits. Auto-stepping allows the character to traverse small obstacles, and <link to="physics_collision" offset="collision_types">Shape-Shape</link> collisions are used to interact with physical objects by applying impulses.</para>
		</brief>
	</desc>
	<controls>
			<![CDATA[
		<p align=left><b>WASD</b> - move.<br/>
		<b>Space</b> - jump.<br/>
		<b>Shift</b> - run.<br/>
		<b>Ctrl</b> - crouch.</p>
			]]>
	</controls>
	<tags>
		<tag>Cameras</tag>
		<tag>Games</tag>
		<tag>Basic Recipes</tag>
	</tags>
	<keywords>Player</keywords>
</sample>